@model CommunityHub.Forms.Steps.ProfileFormModel
@*
    Fields-ONLY partial for the Profile step (REQUIREMENTS §148). Contains NO <form>, no
    page chrome (h1 / intro / message banner), no Save button, no Back-to-hub link — the HOST
    (the standalone /Profile page OR the generic /Forms/Wizard shell) owns those and places
    this partial inside its single <form method="post">. Mobile-first. Field labels are kept
    byte-for-byte from the original Profile page (it never used resx). Bound to
    CommunityHub.Forms.Steps.ProfileFormModel; input names stay flat (FullName / Phone /
    AlternateEmail) so model binding is unchanged for both hosts.
*@
<label for="FullName">Full name</label>
<input type="text" asp-for="FullName" autocomplete="name" maxlength="200" />

@* Read-only identity (email + role) shown right after the name (operator 2026-06-25). *@
<label for="ProfileEmail">Email <span style="font-weight:400;color:#6b7280;">(sign-in identity &mdash; read-only)</span></label>
<input type="email" id="ProfileEmail" value="@Model.Email" disabled />

<label for="ProfileRole">Role <span style="font-weight:400;color:#6b7280;">(set by organizers &mdash; read-only)</span></label>
<input type="text" id="ProfileRole" value="@CommunityHub.Branding.RoleDisplay.Name(Model.Role)" disabled />

@*
    §945a (operator 2026-08-07): *"i enforced only for volunteers the phone otherwise disable so it
    is not mandatory and a shared form"* — phone is REQUIRED of VOLUNTEERS ONLY, which is §262's
    original rule. §945 had briefly widened it to every role.

    🔑 The label is driven by the SAME predicate the server validates and the progress bar reads
    (ProfileCompletion.PhoneRequiredFor), never by a hardcoded word. That is the whole §945 lesson:
    when the page said one thing and the server did another, a speaker saved their profile, was told
    it saved, and watched the step stay incomplete for ever. It is a shared form across roles, so
    this is the one place the difference can be stated correctly.
*@
@{ var phoneRequired = CommunityHub.Core.Forms.ProfileCompletion.PhoneRequiredFor(Model.Role); }
<label for="Phone">
    Phone
    <span style="font-weight:400;color:#6b7280;">(@(phoneRequired ? "required" : "optional"))</span>
</label>
<input type="tel" asp-for="Phone" autocomplete="tel" maxlength="40" required="@phoneRequired" />

@* One additional-email field only (operator 2026-06-25 — the separate "secondary
   CC" field was redundant): an alternate address you can ALSO sign in with.

   §422 — the label now states ALL THREE things this address does. It used to say
   "Alternate sign-in email", which described one of them, so the tasks banner could
   invite someone to "add an alternative email" for reminders, land them on this box,
   and leave them believing they had done something this field did not then do. The
   id="AlternateEmail" is also the banner's link fragment — do not rename it without
   updating _SecondaryEmailBanner. *@
<label for="AlternateEmail">Alternate email <span style="font-weight:400;color:#6b7280;">(optional &mdash; sign in with it, and we&rsquo;ll copy your reminders and calendar invites there too)</span></label>
<input type="email" asp-for="AlternateEmail" autocomplete="email" maxlength="320"
       placeholder="blank = use your main email only" />

@if (Model.IsSpeaker)
{
    @* Speaker details (bio, accreditation, country, photo) moved to the consolidated
       Speaker Details page (operator 2026-06-24).

       §422 — "preferred email" removed from this list. That field left Speaker Details
       on 2026-06-28 and this sentence kept pointing at it, so a speaker looking for
       where their other address lives was sent to a page that no longer has one. The
       alternate address is the box directly above. *@
    <p style="font-size:13px;color:#374151;background:#eef2fb;border-left:4px solid var(--el-darkblue,#1D3380);padding:8px 12px;border-radius:6px;margin:16px 0;">
        Your speaker details (bio, photo, accreditation, country) live on
        <a asp-page="/Speaker/Details">Speaker Details</a>.
    </p>
}
